# Trailing slash is canonical (the emitted pages are directory index files).
# Cloudflare Pages' built-in handling otherwise answers non-slash requests with
# a *temporary* 307 to the slash URL; these explicit permanent 301s consolidate
# the variants so search engines converge on one indexed URL per page quickly.
/services /services/ 301
/info /about/ 301
/info/ /about/ 301
/news /news/ 301
/contact /contact/ 301
/accessibility /accessibility/ 301
/data-processing /data-processing/ 301
/privacy-cookies-policy /privacy-cookies-policy/ 301
/terms-of-use /terms-of-use/ 301
/about /about/ 301

